{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Spread of wings.</b> In the shape of birds, because this creature is pure and spends most of its time in the air without filth. And so we find elsewhere: 'seraphim stood above Him, six wings,' etc." "<b>Above their heads.</b> In the manner of humility and fear — like 'with two he covered his face.'" "<b>And their faces, each toward his brother.</b> These facts prove that they were not made as an image to bow down to. For if there were only one of them, or if the face of one were toward the people and the face of the other toward his brother, there would be an opening for an opponent to say it was made for worship. But now that the faces of both are each toward his brother, and moreover both their faces are turned down toward the cover, the place of the Shekhinah and the Torah, and moreover they were not seen by any creature except the high priest four times on one day in the year — it is well known that they were there only for ornament, like attendants. As it says: 'seraphim stood,' etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:26.779784859Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}